"""Build the lower-bound page after a full exact verification."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import json,hashlib
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
a=json.loads((ROOT/'independent-verification.json').read_text());assert a['fullPolynomialIdentityVerified'] and not a['sharpnessClaimed'];assert a['certificateSha256']==hashlib.sha256((ROOT/'sos-certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()
def tex(t):return '<div class="proof-equation" data-tex="'+escape(t,quote=True)+'"></div>'
s='''<section class="intro"><div class="intro-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Exact rational certificate · 4 November 2026</p><h1>Eleven qubits:<br><em>a tighter lower bound for S<sub>6</sub></em></h1><p class="intro-description">An exact sum-of-squares certificate narrows the remaining optimality gap to less than 0.001244. Equality with the known algebraic candidate remains unproved.</p></div></section><section class="reference-section" id="bound"><h2>The rigorous interval</h2>'''
s+=tex(r'\boxed{\frac{565539}{5000}=113.1078\ \le\ \min_{\psi\in\operatorname{Sym}^{11}(\mathbb C^2)}S_6(\psi)\ \le\ s_\star\simeq113.10904356634669.}')
s+='<p>The minimization is over normalized pure states. The upper endpoint is an exactly attained algebraic number of degree 11. Its isolated root, exact state and stationary equations are supplied in the <a href="../algebraic-s6/index.html#n11">algebraic reconstruction</a>. The lower endpoint is proved below and improves the previous certified bound of 3014/27. This certificate does not establish global optimality of the algebraic representative.</p></section><section class="reference-section" id="proof"><h2>Proof by a degree-eight identity</h2><p>For arbitrary complex Dicke amplitudes, define</p>'
s+=tex(r'c_r=\sqrt{\binom{11}{r}}x_r,\qquad q=\sum_{r=0}^{11}\binom{11}{r}|x_r|^2,\qquad P_6=q^2S_6(\psi/\sqrt q).')
s+='<p>The saved polynomial vectors and positive rational matrices satisfy the exact identity</p>'
s+=tex(r'\boxed{q^2\left(P_6-\frac{565539}{5000}q^2\right)=\sum_{B=1}^{'+str(a['positiveDefiniteGramBlocks'])+r'}\sum_{m=0}^{2L_B}\frac{\mathbf v_{B,m}^{\dagger}G_B\mathbf v_{B,m}}{\binom{2L_B}{m}}\ge0.}')
s+='<p>Each polynomial vector has degree four. All matrices are real symmetric and positive definite, so the right-hand side is nonnegative for every complex state. Since the left-hand side is '+tex(r'q^4\left(S_6(\psi/\sqrt q)-\frac{565539}{5000}\right)')+'and q is positive for every nonzero state, division gives the claimed inequality.</p>'
s+=f'<p>The independent verifier checks all {a["allMonomialsIncludingCancellations"]} coefficients, including cancellations, and proves positivity of all {a["positiveDefiniteGramBlocks"]} Gram matrices by exact leading principal minors. The largest matrix has dimension {a["maxMatrixDimension"]}. Exact LDL decomposition yields {a["squaredForms"]} positively weighted absolute squares.</p>'
s+='<p><a href="basis.json" download>Polynomial vectors ↓</a> · <a href="sos-certificate.json" download>Rational Gram matrices and scales ↓</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json">Verification report and input hashes</a></p><p>In the polynomial file, indices 0–11 denote x<sub>0</sub>,…,x<sub>11</sub>; indices 12–23 denote their conjugates. Each monomial is a list of variable indices. Divide each channel by its corresponding <code>basisScales</code> factor before applying its matrix.</p></section><section class="reference-section" id="derivation"><h2>Independent derivation</h2>'
s+=tex(r'(\rho_t)_{ab}=\sqrt{\binom ta\binom tb}\sum_{j=0}^{11-t}\binom{11-t}{j}x_{a+j}\overline{x_{b+j}},\qquad P_6=462\sum_{t=0}^{6}(-1)^{6-t}\binom6t2^t\operatorname{tr}(\rho_t^2).')
s+='<p>The standalone verifier derives the target from these reduced matrices, independently of the construction of the polynomial basis.</p></section><section class="reference-section" id="verify"><h2>Reproduce the proof</h2><pre>python3 verify_certificate.py</pre><p>The <a href="verify_certificate.py">independent verifier</a> uses only the Python standard library and exact fractions. No solver, tolerance or numerical hypothesis enters the proof. Numerical optimization was used only to discover the matrices.</p></section>'
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Eleven-qubit S6 lower bound · Exact proof</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>.proof-equation{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.4rem 0;padding:.4rem 0}pre{overflow-x:auto;padding:1rem;background:var(--panel,#f0f1eb)}main{max-width:1100px}</style></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="../../index.html#n=11&amp;k=6&amp;mode=min">← Sector-length catalogue</a><nav><a href="#bound">Bound</a><a href="#proof">Proof</a><a href="#verify">Verify</a></nav></header><main>'''+s+'''</main><footer class="site-footer"><a href="../index.html">All proofs and remaining gaps ↗</a></footer><script>document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>document.querySelectorAll('[data-tex]').forEach(el=>{el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:true,throwOnError:false,trust:false})}));</script></body></html>'''
(ROOT/'index.html').write_text(html)
